00:56:35.820 --> 00:56:37.500
So I think online transnational repression

00:56:37.500 --> 00:56:39.203
is particularly interesting

00:56:39.203 --> 00:56:41.990
because essentially costless for a regime.

00:56:41.990 --> 00:56:43.880
The other kinds of
transnational repression

00:56:43.880 --> 00:56:46.110
that I was referring
to, in the case of Ali

00:56:46.110 --> 00:56:49.250
is that they pressure some
of his family back home,

00:56:49.250 --> 00:56:52.090
and then the Egyptian
state has been investing

00:56:52.090 --> 00:56:56.150
and kind of its overseas
repression or surveillance.

00:56:56.150 --> 00:56:58.820
They've been beefing up
the intelligence collection

00:56:58.820 --> 00:56:59.653
at their embassies.

00:56:59.653 --> 00:57:02.630
And what Ali claims in some later videos

00:57:02.630 --> 00:57:06.680
is that he is being trailed
by an Egyptian puja.

00:57:08.189 --> 00:57:09.022
So I think there's a couple things.

00:57:09.022 --> 00:57:12.770
I think the fact that
Sisi responded to him

00:57:12.770 --> 00:57:14.200
made him more credible.

00:57:14.200 --> 00:57:16.663
You see the spikes,
there's clearly a reaction.

00:57:17.630 --> 00:57:19.570
And I think he did so
because the information

00:57:19.570 --> 00:57:22.070
that Ali was putting out
was particularly damning.

00:57:23.690 --> 00:57:28.100
Although that was probably
a badly calculated risk.

00:57:28.100 --> 00:57:29.940
Had he ignored it maybe it
wouldn't have gone viral

00:57:29.940 --> 00:57:30.773
the way it did.

00:57:33.937 --> 00:57:36.890
Yeah I mean, I think regimes
make mistakes on these things,

00:57:36.890 --> 00:57:37.880
they either don't notice,

00:57:37.880 --> 00:57:40.520
or they think it's not that big a deal.

00:57:40.520 --> 00:57:42.530
I think once the 27th happened,

00:57:42.530 --> 00:57:43.950
those were pretty large protests,

00:57:43.950 --> 00:57:45.410
particularly in a country right now

00:57:45.410 --> 00:57:47.473
where tightly repressive.

00:57:48.750 --> 00:57:50.190
After that, I mean, I
think you see the regime

00:57:50.190 --> 00:57:53.810
and then say, okay we
really need to squash this,

00:57:53.810 --> 00:57:55.800
both in terms of physical presence,

00:57:55.800 --> 00:58:00.070
and shutting down those
accounts and trailing Ali.

00:58:00.070 --> 00:58:03.840
So I mean, in some ways this
time periods aren't that long,

00:58:03.840 --> 00:58:07.440
it's between September
2nd, and September 27th

00:58:07.440 --> 00:58:10.210
where we get an
introduction of information,

00:58:10.210 --> 00:58:12.090
and then major protest.

00:58:12.090 --> 00:58:15.703
So I guess they're moving
as quickly as they can.

00:58:16.660 --> 00:58:18.160
That might be part of it, too.

00:58:20.180 --> 00:58:21.043
- [Man] Thank you.

00:58:23.170 --> 00:58:26.100
- [Woman] I have actually
had question as well.

00:58:26.100 --> 00:58:31.100
So it's regarding the ability
of the regime to shut down

00:58:33.180 --> 00:58:37.743
