00:58:56.700 --> 00:59:00.020
whatever the regime is not liking

00:59:03.140 --> 00:59:05.850
and what would be also the reaction

00:59:05.850 --> 00:59:10.420
for the activist themselves,
maybe to transfer to use

00:59:10.420 --> 00:59:14.004
another way of communicating

00:59:14.004 --> 00:59:18.320
that cannot be survey the same point.

00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:23.037
- Yeah, absolutely, so
in terms of the first.

00:59:23.037 --> 00:59:27.480
So the pressure on my
accompany is that in this case

00:59:27.480 --> 00:59:29.430
they shut down.

00:59:29.430 --> 00:59:32.690
They use Twitter if you're
familiar with Twitter,

00:59:32.690 --> 00:59:37.020
you can report content for
various reasons it's offensive,

00:59:37.020 --> 00:59:39.370
or it's politically inflammatory.

00:59:39.370 --> 00:59:41.020
It seems like what the regime

00:59:41.020 --> 00:59:44.770
did was flag Arabic language content,

00:59:44.770 --> 00:59:46.810
said it was inflammatory.

00:59:46.810 --> 00:59:51.810
Twitter immediately removed those accounts

00:59:51.970 --> 00:59:53.800
and that content.

00:59:53.800 --> 00:59:56.650
Eventually, I don't really know

00:59:56.650 --> 00:59:57.760
what goes on behind the scenes,

00:59:57.760 --> 00:59:59.230
but eventually it was reviewed.

00:59:59.230 --> 01:00:01.920
And I found that it wasn't actually

01:00:01.920 --> 01:00:03.890
politically inflammatory

01:00:03.890 --> 01:00:05.743
and so they reinstated the accounts.

01:00:06.750 --> 01:00:08.780
There was also a couple of Twitter threads

01:00:08.780 --> 01:00:12.380
where people were
collecting names of people

01:00:12.380 --> 01:00:13.850
who had been targeted.

01:00:13.850 --> 01:00:15.720
So then there was a sense
of, okay, all these people

01:00:15.720 --> 01:00:18.020
were tweeting about this thing,

01:00:18.020 --> 01:00:19.340
that's not politically inflammatory,

01:00:19.340 --> 01:00:22.040
it's just oppositional information.

01:00:22.040 --> 01:00:24.460
And there was an investigative report done

01:00:24.460 --> 01:00:26.763
by a journalist outside of the country.

01:00:28.511 --> 01:00:33.511
I think I have another graph
here of one additional thing,

01:00:33.960 --> 01:00:37.950
in addition to shutting down the accounts,

01:00:37.950 --> 01:00:40.253
the Egyptian state.

01:00:42.140 --> 01:00:47.140
Let me see, no, I don't have it.

01:00:49.960 --> 01:00:50.800
They are able

01:00:50.800 --> 01:00:55.270
to basically make certain
websites unavailable.

01:00:55.270 --> 01:00:58.843
And you can see access
to Twitter and Facebook,

01:00:59.910 --> 01:01:00.927
if I had the graph you could see

01:01:00.927 --> 01:01:04.020
but it's basically limited by 20 to 30%,

01:01:04.020 --> 01:01:05.500
at different moments.

01:01:05.500 --> 01:01:07.780
So they're able to do it on
a couple different levels.

01:01:07.780 --> 01:01:11.450
But this investigative
journalist demonstrated,

01:01:11.450 --> 01:01:12.710
it wasn't because they were saying

01:01:12.710 --> 01:01:15.250
something like use violence or whatever

01:01:15.250 --> 01:01:18.150
it was really, they were just
retweeting this information.

01:01:19.380 --> 01:01:22.400
And I do think what I
really enjoy about activists

01:01:22.400 --> 01:01:24.390
is that we're able to use sources

01:01:24.390 --> 01:01:27.570
from a bunch of different platforms,

01:01:27.570 --> 01:01:30.100
or data from a number
of different sources.

01:01:30.100 --> 01:01:32.955
We do see that these things
are happening in tandem,

01:01:32.955 --> 01:01:35.008
so there's a lot of
the information cascade

01:01:35.008 --> 01:01:37.327
is happening across different platforms.

01:01:37.327 --> 01:01:40.067
Obviously there's also secret ways to talk

01:01:40.067 --> 01:01:42.048
about this stuff, WhatsApp and Signal

01:01:42.048 --> 01:01:43.456
they're obviously doing that as well.

01:01:43.456 --> 01:01:48.456
It's just harder to find public
data on that kind of stuff.

01:01:48.460 --> 01:01:49.620
There's been some interesting papers

01:01:49.620 --> 01:01:52.510
on also like Telegram and Clubhouse

01:01:52.510 --> 01:01:55.603
ways that people when the
internet gets shut down,

01:01:56.450 --> 01:01:57.580
when Facebook gets shut down,

01:01:57.580 --> 01:02:01.100
when Twitter's being
monitored using Clubhouse

01:02:01.100 --> 01:02:03.270
can sometimes be an alternative to that.

01:02:03.270 --> 01:02:04.630
So they're definitely being strategic

01:02:04.630 --> 01:02:05.923
in terms of that as well.

01:02:09.160 --> 01:02:14.160
But their regime have they shut down,

01:02:15.050 --> 01:02:18.690
or what is their approach
to these companies

01:02:18.690 --> 01:02:20.717
working inside the (indistinct).

